WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.482
Flow for OpenCode is a workflow

2
00:00:02.482 --> 00:00:04.964
plugin with a very small core.

3
00:00:04.964 --> 00:00:07.446
It does not try to make

4
00:00:07.446 --> 00:00:09.927
every judgment in TypeScript. Instead, it

5
00:00:09.927 --> 00:00:12.409
saves the facts that must survive

6
00:00:12.409 --> 00:00:14.891
restarts. The repository ships one npm

7
00:00:14.891 --> 00:00:17.373
package, opencode-plugin-flow. It adds slash commands

8
00:00:17.373 --> 00:00:19.855
, hidden worker agents, managed skills, and

9
00:00:19.855 --> 00:00:22.337
seven runtime tools. Together they turn

10
00:00:22.337 --> 00:00:24.819
a large coding goal into an

11
00:00:24.819 --> 00:00:27.300
approved plan, one feature at a

12
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:29.782
time. The main split is simple.

13
00:00:29.782 --> 00:00:32.264
The skills directory owns judgment. Source

14
00:00:32.264 --> 00:00:34.746
files under src own safety. That

15
00:00:34.746 --> 00:00:37.228
split is written into the maintainer

16
00:00:37.228 --> 00:00:39.710
contract and ADR 0001. If a

17
00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:42.191
rule needs interpretation, it belongs in

18
00:00:42.191 --> 00:00:44.673
a skill. If a rule must

19
00:00:44.673 --> 00:00:47.155
never be bypassed, it belongs in

20
00:00:47.155 --> 00:00:49.637
the runtime. Startup begins in src

21
00:00:49.637 --> 00:00:52.119
index dot ts. That file exports

22
00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:54.601
the OpenCode adapter from src adapters

23
00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:57.083
opencode plugin dot ts. The adapter

24
00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:59.564
syncs managed skills, registers config, registers

25
00:00:59.564 --> 00:01:02.046
tools, and rewrites Flow command bodies

26
00:01:02.046 --> 00:01:04.528
before they run. This is how

27
00:01:04.528 --> 00:01:07.010
public commands stay current even when

28
00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.492
native skill discovery is stale. The

29
00:01:09.492 --> 00:01:11.974
runtime API is the controlled doorway

30
00:01:11.974 --> 00:01:14.456
into state. Tool handlers parse Zod

31
00:01:14.456 --> 00:01:16.937
schemas, lock the workspace, load the

32
00:01:16.937 --> 00:01:19.419
current session, call a pure transition

33
00:01:19.419 --> 00:01:21.901
, and then save or archive the

34
00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:24.383
result. The seven tool names are

35
00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:26.865
flow status, flow plan save, flow

36
00:01:26.865 --> 00:01:29.347
plan approve, flow run start, flow

37
00:01:29.347 --> 00:01:31.829
feature complete, flow feature reset, and

38
00:01:31.829 --> 00:01:34.310
flow session close. The session model

39
00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.792
is the key primitive. It records

40
00:01:36.792 --> 00:01:39.274
the goal, current status, approval state

41
00:01:39.274 --> 00:01:41.756
, plan, active feature, history, closure, last

42
00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:44.238
error, and timestamps. Plans contain requirements

43
00:01:44.238 --> 00:01:46.720
, decisions, a final review policy, and

44
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.201
feature entries. Features use lowercase kebab

45
00:01:49.201 --> 00:01:51.683
case ids, dependency lists, targets, validation

46
00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:54.165
hints, and explicit status. The state

47
00:01:54.165 --> 00:01:56.647
machine is intentionally strict. A plan

48
00:01:56.647 --> 00:01:59.129
can be saved while a session

49
00:01:59.129 --> 00:02:01.611
is planning. Once approved, the plan

50
00:02:01.611 --> 00:02:04.093
is locked. Only one feature can

51
00:02:04.093 --> 00:02:06.574
be in progress. Dependencies must be

52
00:02:06.574 --> 00:02:09.056
complete before a feature can start.

53
00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:11.538
Blocked features have to be reset

54
00:02:11.538 --> 00:02:14.020
before they run again. Completion is

55
00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.502
where Flow draws the hard line.

56
00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.984
Every completed feature needs passing validation

57
00:02:18.984 --> 00:02:21.466
evidence and a passing feature review.

58
00:02:21.466 --> 00:02:23.947
Ordinary features use targeted validation. The

59
00:02:23.947 --> 00:02:26.429
final feature uses broad validation and

60
00:02:26.429 --> 00:02:28.911
also needs a final review. The

61
00:02:28.911 --> 00:02:31.393
final review depth must match the

62
00:02:31.393 --> 00:02:33.875
approved plan policy. Persistence lives under

63
00:02:33.875 --> 00:02:36.357
dot flow. The active ledger is

64
00:02:36.357 --> 00:02:38.839
dot flow slash session dot json.

65
00:02:38.839 --> 00:02:41.320
Closed sessions move to dot flow

66
00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.802
slash history. The generated OpenCode instruction

67
00:02:43.802 --> 00:02:46.284
file is a projection, not a

68
00:02:46.284 --> 00:02:48.766
source of truth. Workspace code writes

69
00:02:48.766 --> 00:02:51.248
atomically, uses a session lock, rejects

70
00:02:51.248 --> 00:02:53.730
unsafe roots, and quarantines unreadable sessions

71
00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:56.212
instead of deleting them. Managed skills

72
00:02:56.212 --> 00:02:58.693
make the plugin installable. The distribution

73
00:02:58.693 --> 00:03:01.175
layer imports markdown from skills slash

74
00:03:01.175 --> 00:03:03.657
flow, flow plan, flow run, flow

75
00:03:03.657 --> 00:03:06.139
test, flow review, flow deslop, flow

76
00:03:06.139 --> 00:03:08.621
UI quality, and flow commit. Sync

77
00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:11.103
writes marked skill folders into the

78
00:03:11.103 --> 00:03:13.584
OpenCode skills root. Doctor reports distinguish

79
00:03:13.584 --> 00:03:16.066
missing, outdated, edited, and foreign folders.

80
00:03:16.066 --> 00:03:18.548
Parallel orchestration is available, but state

81
00:03:18.548 --> 00:03:21.030
remains serial. Hidden workers can gather

82
00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.512
evidence, validate commands, audit findings, review

83
00:03:23.512 --> 00:03:25.994
slices, propose candidate patches, or verify

84
00:03:25.994 --> 00:03:28.476
claims. Their permission maps deny Flow

85
00:03:28.476 --> 00:03:30.957
state changing tools. The manager checks

86
00:03:30.957 --> 00:03:33.439
their handoffs and owns every state

87
00:03:33.439 --> 00:03:35.921
transition. The test suite mirrors the

88
00:03:35.921 --> 00:03:38.403
boundaries. Runtime gates cover planning, dependencies

89
00:03:38.403 --> 00:03:40.885
, completion, blockers, reset, and final review

90
00:03:40.885 --> 00:03:43.367
policy. Workspace tests cover JSON parsing

91
00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:45.849
, locks, generated instructions, archive, and quarantine.

92
00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:48.330
Distribution and surface tests cover commands

93
00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:50.812
, agents, skill sync, permissions, setup health

94
00:03:50.812 --> 00:03:53.294
, and bounded recovery. The release path

95
00:03:53.294 --> 00:03:55.776
is also guarded. Continuous integration runs

96
00:03:55.776 --> 00:03:58.258
typecheck, Biome, build, and tests across

97
00:03:58.258 --> 00:04:00.740
Node versions and operating systems. The

98
00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:03.222
release workflow checks tag and changelog

99
00:04:03.222 --> 00:04:05.703
consistency, runs package smoke, packs the

100
00:04:05.703 --> 00:04:08.185
tarball, records a checksum, publishes to

101
00:04:08.185 --> 00:04:10.667
npm, and updates GitHub release assets.

102
00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:13.149
You can remember the repository as

103
00:04:13.149 --> 00:04:15.631
three layers. OpenCode integration wires Flow

104
00:04:15.631 --> 00:04:18.113
into the host. The runtime ledger

105
00:04:18.113 --> 00:04:20.594
preserves safety and state. The skills

106
00:04:20.594 --> 00:04:23.076
bundle supplies the operating judgment. That

107
00:04:23.076 --> 00:04:25.558
is why Flow can be resumable

108
00:04:25.558 --> 00:04:28.040
and strict without turning the runtime

109
00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:30.108
into a large planning framework.
